Marut Drones — Precision Landing on Moving Platform
Complete Project Documentation
1. Project Overview
Goal
Build an autonomous drone that can land precisely on an AprilTag marker placed on either:

A stationary platform (proven and tested ✓)
A moving ground rover (in development)
Use Cases
Drone delivery onto moving vehicles (defense, logistics)
Autonomous drone recovery on USVs (boats)
Static pad precision landing for charging/return-to-base
Accuracy Target
Stationary tag: ~5–10 cm
Rover at 0.5 m/s: ~15–25 cm
Rover at 1 m/s: ~25–40 cm
