7. MAVLink Protocol
Messages Sent by Pi → Drone Cube
Message	Rate	Purpose
LANDING_TARGET	20 Hz	Visual angle to tag
SET_POSITION_TARGET_LOCAL_NED	30 Hz	Velocity commands
COMMAND_LONG (DO_SET_MODE)	as needed	Mode changes
COMMAND_LONG (ARM_DISARM)	one-shot	Touchdown disarm
HEARTBEAT	1 Hz	Pi alive signal (comp=191)
Messages Read by Pi
Message	Source	Field used
HEARTBEAT (sysid=1, comp=1)	Drone autopilot	armed, mode
ATTITUDE (sysid=1, comp=1)	Drone autopilot	yaw
VFR_HUD (sysid=1, comp=1)	Drone autopilot	altitude, climb_rate
GLOBAL_POSITION_INT (sysid=1)	Drone autopilot	lat, lon (for GPS-NAV)
GLOBAL_POSITION_INT (sysid=2)	Rover	lat, lon, vx, vy, vz
LANDING_TARGET Payload

time_usec      : microseconds since epoch
target_num     : 0
frame          : MAV_FRAME_BODY_FRD (12)
angle_x        : atan2(forward, distance) — radians
angle_y        : atan2(right, distance) — radians
distance       : 3D distance to tag — meters
8. Installation Procedure
Step 1: Raspberry Pi Setup

# Install system packages
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y python3-picamera2 python3-opencv python3-numpy git

# Create Python venv with system packages
python3 -m venv --system-site-packages ~/precland
source ~/precland/bin/activate

# Install Pi-side packages
pip install pupil-apriltags pymavlink

# Add user to dialout group
sudo usermod -aG dialout marut

# Enable serial port if using UART
sudo raspi-config nonint do_serial_hw 0
Step 2: Camera Calibration

source ~/precland/bin/activate
python ~/calibrate.py    # uses checkerboard
# Verify RMS reprojection error < 0.5
Step 3: Print AprilTag

python ~/make_tag.py 0   # generates tag36h11_0.png
# Print at 100% scale on matte paper
# Measure black square edge with ruler
# Set TAG_SIZE in config.py to measured value (in meters)
Step 4: Install systemd Service

sudo cp ~/precland.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now precland.service
Step 5: Configure Cubes
Load marut_drone.parm on drone Cube
Load marut_rover.parm on rover Cube
Reboot both
Step 6: Set Up Communication (SiK or RC TX backchannel)
Wire radios to TELEM ports
Pair SiK radios in Mission Planner (if using SiK)
Enable MAVLink mode on RC TXs (if using backchannel)
9. Operation Procedures
Pre-Flight Checklist

☐ Battery charged (drone + rover)
☐ Calibration.json present on Pi
☐ AprilTag printed and mounted flat on rover
☐ Mission Planner sees both vehicles
☐ Drone GPS lock obtained
☐ Rover GPS lock obtained
☐ Pi logs show rover=True
☐ Pre-arm checks pass on drone
☐ Safety pilot briefed
☐ RC mode switch positioned at LOITER
☐ Open area, no people
Boot Sequence

T=0       Battery plugged → Cubes start booting
T=5       SiK radios link (if used)
T=10      Pi boots Linux
T=30      precland.service starts
T=40      Script initialized; "Moving-platform precision landing — pilot-engaged via GUIDED"
T=45      Mission Planner sees both vehicles
T=50      rover=True visible in Pi log
T=60+     Ready to arm
Flight Sequence

1. Pilot arms drone in LOITER
2. Take off, climb to ~5 m
3. Position drone roughly above rover (or near rover)
4. Release sticks → LOITER holds position
5. PILOT: Flip RC switch to GUIDED ← engagement
6. Script logs ">>> Pilot engaged GUIDED — script taking over"
7. Script computes vx, vy, vz commands
   - MODE A if tag visible: visual + rover velocity FF
   - MODE B if no tag, rover GPS available: fly toward rover
   - MODE C if nothing: hover
8. Drone autonomously approaches and descends
9. Touchdown detected → auto-disarm
Abort
At any time during APPROACH:

Pilot RC switch to LOITER/POSHOLD/RTL
Script returns to IDLE
Pilot has full RC control
