11. Safety Features
Built-in Safety
Feature	Behavior
Pilot mode override	RC switch out of GUIDED → script stops immediately
GUID_TIMEOUT (3s)	Drone hovers if Pi script crashes
ABORT_LOST_TIMEOUT (15s)	Hover/warn if tag and rover both lost
Velocity caps	All commands clamped to ±2 m/s XY, ±0.8 m/s Z
Force-disarm on touchdown	Uses magic number 21196 to bypass safety
BENCH_MODE	Hover-only mode for bench testing
Hard Operational Rules

1. Safety pilot ALWAYS present with finger on RC mode switch
2. Test progressively: stationary → walking → 0.5 m/s → 1 m/s
3. Open area minimum 20 m radius, no people, no obstacles
4. Verify axis signs (FLIP_FWD/RIGHT/SWAP_AXES) on bench before flight
5. Battery > 70% for landing tests
6. Camera focus locked mechanically
12. Troubleshooting
Symptom	Cause	Fix
"Waiting for heartbeat..." hang	Wrong device, wrong baud	Check ls /dev/ttyACM*, verify baud=115200
precland.service crash loop	Python exception	journalctl -u precland.service -n 50
raw_dets = 0	Camera focus, print quality	Re-focus lens, reprint matte
rover=False always	Rover SYSID wrong, link broken	Set SYSID=2, check SiK/RC link
armed=False blocks trigger	Safety gate working as designed	Force-arm in MP (props off) for bench
Drone oscillates near tag	KP_XY too high or latency	Lower KP_XY to 0.8 or 1.0
Mode flickers in HUD	Multiple component HEARTBEATs	Already filtered (comp=1 only)
Mission Planner shows two sys=1 entries	Rover SYSID not set	Change rover SYSID_THISMAV=2
Pose estimation ambiguous near landing	IPPE-square ambiguity	Add IPPE_SQUARE pose solver
Tag too small to detect at altitude	Tag size vs distance	Add nested tag bundle
Glare blows out detection	Glossy print	Use matte print spec
LANDING_TARGET arrives late	Wrong time_usec	Use actual capture timestamp
